\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The Lord will come, and not be slow;
\par His footsteps cannot err;
\par Before Him righteousness shall go,
\par His royal harbinger.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Truth from the earth, like to a flower,
\par Shall bud and blossom then;
\par And justice, from her heavenly bower,
\par Look down on mortal men.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Rise, Lord, judge Thou the earth in might,
\par This longing earth redress;
\par For Thou art He who shall by right
\par The nations all possess.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The nations all whom Thou hast made
\par Shall come, and all shall frame
\par To bow them low before Thee, Lord, 
\par And glorify Thy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For great Thou art, and wonders great
\par By Thy strong hand are done;
\par Thou in Thine everlasting seat
\par Remainest God alone.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

